{"id":4059,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/","parentId":540,"order":150,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Past simple: Negatives and questions","seo":{"title":"Past simple: Negatives and questions - Test-English","description":"Learn how to form past simple negatives and questions in this A1 Elementary grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_Past-simple_Negatives-and-questions.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T18:02:31","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct past simple forms to complete the sentences below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"468\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct past simple forms to complete these sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"469\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete the conversation using the words in brackets to make past simple positive, negative, and questions.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"470\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Past simple negatives and questions</h2> <p>We use <strong>did&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong>didn’t</strong> to make negatives, questions and short answers in past simple.<br> <br> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-18804\" src=\"/media/uploads/past-simple_form_new.jpg\" alt=\"Grammar chart outlining the structure of the past simple tense in positive, negative, and question forms, with examples and common mistakes.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4>Word order in questions</h4> <p>Remember that the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/questions/\">word order in questions</a> is <strong>QWASI</strong>: (Question Word), Auxiliary (did), Subject, Infinitive.<br> <br> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-18805\" src=\"/media/uploads/Past-simple-questions.jpg\" alt=\"Grammar chart demonstrating how to form questions in the past simple tense using 'was/were' with 'be' and 'did' with other verbs.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4>Infinitive without&nbsp;<strong>to</strong></h4> <p>We use <strong>did</strong>&nbsp;or <strong>didn’t</strong> with the <strong>bare infinitive</strong> of the main verb (= infinitive without&nbsp;<strong>to</strong>).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>didn’t</strong></span> <span><strong>work</strong></span> yesterday.</em> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I didn’t <span><strong>didn’t worked</strong></span> yesterday. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Did</strong></span> you <span><strong>go</strong></span> to the concert?</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em><strong><span>Did</span></strong> you <span><strong>went</strong></span> to the concert? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4>Don’t use&nbsp;<strong>did</strong> in positive sentences</h4> <p>We use&nbsp;<strong>did</strong>&nbsp;or <strong>didn’t</strong> in negatives, questions and short answers, but <strong>NOT in positive sentences</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We <span><strong>stayed</strong></span> home yesterday.&nbsp;</em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>did stay</strong></span> home yesterday. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>went</strong></span> out last night. </em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>did go</strong></span> out last night. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Did</strong> or <strong>was/were</strong>?</h4> <p>We use <strong>did</strong> and <strong>didn’t</strong> (NOT <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/was-were/\"><strong>was/wasn’t</strong> or <strong>were/weren’t</strong></a>) as the auxiliary verb in negatives and questions in past simple.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We <span><strong>didn’t eat</strong></span> at 6.&nbsp;</em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>weren’t eat</strong></span> at 6. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Did</strong></span> you <span><strong>do</strong></span> your homework?</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em><span><strong>Were</strong></span>&nbsp;you <span><strong>do</strong></span> your homework? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <p>We do <strong>NOT </strong>use<strong>&nbsp;did </strong>or&nbsp;<strong>didn’t</strong>&nbsp;in past simple negatives or questions when the <strong>main verb</strong> is&nbsp;<strong>be</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>They <span><strong>weren’t</strong></span> happy.</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>They <span><strong>didn’t be</strong></span> happy. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Was</strong></span> he at home?</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em><span><strong>Did</strong></span> he <span><strong>be</strong></span> at home? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":468,"questions":[{"id":4082,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> on holiday last summer?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["did you go","went you","did you went"]}]},{"id":4083,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> until 5 o'clock in the afternoon.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't arrive","weren't arrived","didn't arrived"]}]},{"id":4094,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> sure of what to do.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't be","didn't were","weren't"]}]},{"id":4095,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> after midnight.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["did arrive","didn't arrived","arrived"]}]},{"id":4096,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the present?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["did you liked","Were you like","Did you like"]}]},{"id":4097,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Sara <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the film because she was asleep. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't watched","weren't watch","didn't watch"]}]},{"id":4098,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>John and Felicity <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> married last year. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["got","were get","did get"]}]},{"id":4099,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> ready for the test. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't was","wasn't","didn't be"]}]},{"id":4100,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the question. Can you repeat it?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["wasn't understood","didn't understand","didn't understood"]}]},{"id":4101,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> when he saw you?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Did he smiled","Did he smile","Was he smile"]}]}]},{"id":469,"questions":[{"id":4084,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We _____ a bus to Chicago last week.</div>","choices":[{"id":5952,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>were took</span>"},{"id":5953,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>did took</span>"},{"id":5954,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>took</span>"}]},{"id":4085,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ to the party last weekend?</div>","choices":[{"id":5955,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Did you go</span>"},{"id":5956,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Went you</span>"},{"id":5957,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Did you went</span>"}]},{"id":4086,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Yesterday I ____ the train, but I ____ late for work.</div>","choices":[{"id":5958,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did miss / were not</span>"},{"id":5959,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>missed / didn't be</span>"},{"id":5960,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>missed / wasn't</span>"}]},{"id":4087,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They _____ a swimming pool in their backyard last summer.</div>","choices":[{"id":5961,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did put</span>"},{"id":5962,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>putted</span>"},{"id":5963,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>put</span>"}]},{"id":4088,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Where _____ this afternoon?</div>","choices":[{"id":5964,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>were he go</span>"},{"id":5965,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>did he go</span>"},{"id":5966,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>did he went</span>"}]},{"id":4089,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She _____ home early from the party yesterday.</div>","choices":[{"id":5967,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>came</span>"},{"id":5968,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>camed</span>"},{"id":5969,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>didn't came</span>"}]},{"id":4090,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>How much _____ for it?</div>","choices":[{"id":5970,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did you paid </span>"},{"id":5971,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>did you pay</span>"},{"id":5972,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>paid you</span>"}]},{"id":4091,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They _____ the play very much.</div>","choices":[{"id":5973,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>weren't enjoy</span>"},{"id":5974,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>didn't enjoyed</span>"},{"id":5975,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>didn't enjoy</span>"}]},{"id":4092,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>When _____ that crazy idea?</div>","choices":[{"id":5976,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did you got</span>"},{"id":5977,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>did you get</span>"},{"id":5978,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>got you</span>"}]},{"id":4093,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Where _____ last night?</div>","choices":[{"id":5979,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>were you</span>"},{"id":5980,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>did you be</span>"},{"id":5981,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>did you were</span>"}]}]},{"id":470,"questions":[{"id":4102,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Emma: Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/travel) this summer?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4103,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Phil: We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (go) to Playa del Carmen, in Mexico. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4104,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Emma: Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/stay)?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4105,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Phil: We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (stay) in a nice beach resort.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4106,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Emma: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (your children/like) it?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4107,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Phil: Of course! They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (spend) all week on the beach.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4108,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Emma: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (be/you) there for one week?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4109,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Phil: Yes. We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (come) back last Sunday.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4110,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Emma: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (your wife/enjoy) the trip too?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4111,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Phil: Yes, she <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>, although she <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> (not like) the food too much.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}